{"id":"mahabharata-5-147","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":147,"title":"सप्तचत्वारिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 147 · Dhritarashtra's history of the throne","summary":{"en":"Krishna reports Dhritarashtra's words: he recounted the history of the Kuru throne, how the elder Devapi was passed over for his skin disease, how Pandu ruled while he himself was blind, and that the kingdom therefore belongs to Pandu's sons. He urged Duryodhana to give half the kingdom to the Pandavas.","kn":"ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನ ಮಾತನ್ನು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ತಿಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ: ಚರ್ಮರೋಗದಿಂದ ಹಿರಿಯ ದೇವಾಪಿಯನ್ನು ಬಿಟ್ಟದ್ದು, ತಾನು ಕುರುಡನಾಗಿದ್ದಾಗ ಪಾಂಡು ಆಳಿದ್ದು ಮುಂತಾದ ಕುರುಸಿಂಹಾಸನದ ಇತಿಹಾಸ ಹೇಳಿ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ರಾಜ್ಯ ಪಾಂಡುಪುತ್ರರದು ಎಂದನು. ಅರ್ಧರಾಜ್ಯವನ್ನು ಪಾಂಡವರಿಗೆ ಕೊಡೆಂದು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನನ್ನು ಒತ್ತಾಯಿಸಿದನು.","hi":"श्रीकृष्ण धृतराष्ट्र के वचन बताते हैं: उन्होंने कुरु सिंहासन का इतिहास सुनाया, कैसे बड़े देवापि को चर्मरोग के कारण छोड़ा गया, कैसे उनके अन्धे होने पर पाण्डु ने राज्य किया, और इसलिए राज्य पाण्डु के पुत्रों का है। उन्होंने दुर्योधन से आधा राज्य पाण्डवों को देने का आग्रह किया।","te":"ధృతరాష్ట్రుని మాటలను శ్రీకృష్ణుడు వివరిస్తాడు: చర్మవ్యాధి వల్ల పెద్దవాడైన దేవాపిని పక్కనపెట్టడం, తాను గుడ్డివాడు కావడంతో పాండువు పాలించడం వంటి కురుసింహాసన చరిత్ర చెప్పి, అందువల్ల రాజ్యం పాండుపుత్రులదేనని అన్నాడు. అర్ధరాజ్యాన్ని పాండవులకు ఇవ్వమని దుర్యోధనుని కోరాడు.","ta":"த்ருதராஷ்டிரனின் சொற்களை ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் தெரிவிக்கிறார்: தோல் நோயால் மூத்தவன் தேவாபி விலக்கப்பட்டது, தான் பார்வையற்றவனாக இருந்ததால் பாண்டு ஆண்டது என்று குரு அரியணையின் வரலாற்றைச் சொல்லி, அதனால் அரசு பாண்டுவின் மைந்தர்களுக்கு உரியது என்றான். பாதி அரசைப் பாண்டவர்களுக்குக் கொடுக்குமாறு துரியோதனனை வற்புறுத்தினான்.","ml":"ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രരുടെ വാക്കുകൾ കൃഷ്ണൻ അറിയിക്കുന്നു: കുരുസിംഹാസനത്തിന്റെ ചരിത്രം അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിച്ചു; ത്വക്ക് രോഗം കാരണം മൂത്തവനായ ദേവാപി പിന്തള്ളപ്പെട്ടതും, താൻ അന്ധനായിരുന്നപ്പോൾ പാണ്ഡു ഭരിച്ചതും, അതിനാൽ രാജ്യം പാണ്ഡുവിന്റെ മക്കൾക്കാണെന്നും പറഞ്ഞു. പാണ്ഡവർക്ക് രാജ്യത്തിന്റെ പകുതി നൽകാൻ അദ്ദേഹം ദുര്യോധനനോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെട്ടു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.147; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"अभिनिर्याणपर्व","titleEn":"Abhiniryana Parva (The marching out)","verses":[{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्ते तु गान्धार्या धृतराष्ट्रो जनेश्वरः ।\nदुर्योधनमुवाचेदं नृपमध्ये जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Gandhari had spoken thus, King Dhritarashtra, lord of the people, spoke to Duryodhana in the midst of the kings."}},{"n":2,"text":"दुर्योधन निबोधेदं यत्त्वां वक्ष्यामि पुत्रक ।\nतथा तत्कुरु भद्रं ते यद्यस्ति पितृगौरवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Duryodhana, my son, listen to what I will tell you, and do it, if you have any respect for your father; may good come to you."}},{"n":3,"text":"सोमः प्रजापतिः पूर्वं कुरूणां वंशवर्धनः ।\nसोमाद्बभूव षष्ठो वै ययातिर्नहुषात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago Soma Prajapati increased the line of the Kurus. The sixth from Soma was Yayati, son of Nahusha."}},{"n":4,"text":"तस्य पुत्रा बभूवुश्च पञ्च राजर्षिसत्तमाः ।\nतेषां यदुर्महातेजा ज्येष्ठः समभवत्प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He had five sons, the best of royal sages, and of them great-spirited Yadu was the eldest and the lord."}},{"n":5,"text":"पूरुर्यवीयांश्च ततो योऽस्माकं वंशवर्धनः ।\nशर्मिष्ठायाः संप्रसूतो दुहितुर्वृषपर्वणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Puru was the youngest, who increased our line, born of Sharmishtha, daughter of Vrishaparva."}},{"n":6,"text":"यदुश्च भरतश्रेष्ठ देवयान्याः सुतोऽभवत् ।\nदौहित्रस्तात शुक्रस्य काव्यस्यामिततेजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yadu, best of the Bharatas, was the son of Devayani, grandson of Shukra, the immeasurably brilliant Kavya."}},{"n":7,"text":"यादवानां कुलकरो बलवान्वीर्यसंमतः ।\nअवमेने स तु क्षत्रं दर्पपूर्णः सुमन्दधीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Founder of the Yadava line, strong and honored for his valor, he nevertheless despised the kshatriya order, full of pride and very dull in mind."}},{"n":8,"text":"न चातिष्ठत्पितुः शास्त्रे बलदर्पविमोहितः ।\nअवमेने च पितरं भ्रातॄंश्चाप्यपराजितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bewildered by pride in his strength, he did not stand by his father's teaching, and, thinking himself unconquerable, he looked down on his father and brothers."}},{"n":9,"text":"पृथिव्यां चतुरन्तायां यदुरेवाभवद्बली ।\nवशे कृत्वा स नृपतीनवसन्नागसाह्वये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yadu alone was mighty on earth bounded by four seas; he subdued the kings and lived at Nagasahvaya."}},{"n":10,"text":"तं पिता परमक्रुद्धो ययातिर्नहुषात्मजः ।\nशशाप पुत्रं गान्धारे राज्याच्च व्यपरोपयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yayati, son of Nahusha, his father, greatly angered, cursed his son, son of Gandhari, and removed him from the kingdom."}},{"n":11,"text":"य चैनमन्ववर्तन्त भ्रातरो बलदर्पितम् ।\nशशाप तानपि क्रुद्धो ययातिस्तनयानथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The brothers who followed Yadu in his pride of strength were cursed too, in his anger, by Yayati, those sons."}},{"n":12,"text":"यवीयांसं ततः पूरुं पुत्रं स्ववशवर्तिनम् ।\nराज्ये निवेशयामास विधेयं नृपसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that best of kings set on the throne his youngest son Puru, who obeyed his will and was dutiful."}},{"n":13,"text":"एवं ज्येष्ठोऽप्यथोत्सिक्तो न राज्यमभिजायते ।\nयवीयांसोऽभिजायन्ते राज्यं वृद्धोपसेवया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus even the eldest, if puffed up, does not inherit the kingdom; the younger sons inherit the kingdom by serving their elders."}},{"n":14,"text":"तथैव सर्वधर्मज्ञः पितुर्मम पितामहः ।\nप्रतीपः पृथिवीपालस्त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way my father's grandfather, Pratipa, who knew all dharma and was famed in the three worlds, protector of the earth,"}},{"n":15,"text":"तस्य पार्थिवसिंहस्य राज्यं धर्मेण शासतः ।\nत्रयः प्रजज्ञिरे पुत्रा देवकल्पा यशस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"ruling his kingdom by dharma, that lion among kings, had three glorious sons, like gods."}},{"n":16,"text":"देवापिरभवज्ज्येष्ठो बाह्लीकस्तदनन्तरम् ।\nतृतीयः शंतनुस्तात धृतिमान्मे पितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devapi was the eldest, then Bahlika, and the third, my son, was Shantanu, my steadfast grandfather."}},{"n":17,"text":"देवापिस्तु महातेजास्त्वग्दोषी राजसत्तमः ।\nधार्मिकः सत्यवादी च पितुः शुश्रूषणे रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Devapi, of great splendor, best of kings, was afflicted with a skin disease; he was righteous, truthful, and devoted to serving his father."}},{"n":18,"text":"पौरजानपदानां च संमतः साधुसत्कृतः ।\nसर्वेषां बालवृद्धानां देवापिर्हृदयंगमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was esteemed by townspeople and countrymen, honored by the good, and dear to the hearts of all, young and old."}},{"n":19,"text":"प्राज्ञश्च सत्यसंधश्च सर्वभूतहिते रतः ।\nवर्तमानः पितुः शास्त्रे ब्राह्मणानां तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wise, true to his word, devoted to the good of all beings, he lived by his father's teaching and the brahmins' counsel."}},{"n":20,"text":"बाह्लीकस्य प्रियो भ्राता शंतनोश्च महात्मनः ।\nसौभ्रात्रं च परं तेषां सहितानां महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was the beloved brother of Bahlika and of great-souled Shantanu, and those great souls had very fine brotherhood together."}},{"n":21,"text":"अथ कालस्य पर्याये वृद्धो नृपतिसत्तमः ।\nसंभारानभिषेकार्थं कारयामास शास्त्रतः ।\nमङ्गलानि च सर्वाणि कारयामास चाभिभूः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in the course of time the old king, best of kings, had the materials for the consecration gathered according to the scriptures, and had all the auspicious rites done as well."}},{"n":22,"text":"तं ब्राह्मणाश्च वृद्धाश्च पौरजानपदैः सह ।\nसर्वे निवारयामासुर्देवापेरभिषेचनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the brahmins and elders, with townspeople and countrymen, all prevented Devapi's consecration."}},{"n":23,"text":"स तच्छ्रुत्वा तु नृपतिरभिषेकनिवारणम् ।\nअश्रुकण्ठोऽभवद्राजा पर्यशोचत चात्मजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that his consecration was blocked, the king's throat filled with tears, and he grieved for his son."}},{"n":24,"text":"एवं वदान्यो धर्मज्ञः सत्यसंधश्च सोऽभवत् ।\nप्रियः प्रजानामपि संस्त्वग्दोषेण प्रदूषितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So he was generous, knew dharma and was true to his word, and dear to the people, yet he was marred by the skin disease."}},{"n":25,"text":"हीनाङ्गं पृथिवीपालं नाभिनन्दन्ति देवताः ।\nइति कृत्वा नृपश्रेष्ठं प्रत्यषेधन्द्विजर्षभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They said: \"The gods do not approve of a king with a defective body,\" and so the best of brahmins prevented that best of kings."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततः प्रव्यथितात्मासौ पुत्रशोकसमन्वितः ।\nममार तं मृतं दृष्ट्वा देवापिः संश्रितो वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, distressed in mind and overcome by sorrow for his son, the king died; and seeing his father dead, Devapi took refuge in the forest."}},{"n":27,"text":"बाह्लीको मातुलकुले त्यक्त्वा राज्यं व्यवस्थितः ।\nपितृभ्रातॄन्परित्यज्य प्राप्तवान्पुरमृद्धिमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bahlika gave up the kingdom and settled in his mother's family; leaving his father's brothers, he reached a prosperous city."}},{"n":28,"text":"बाह्लीकेन त्वनुज्ञातः शंतनुर्लोकविश्रुतः ।\nपितर्युपरते राजन्राजा राज्यमकारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With Bahlika's leave, famed Shantanu became king after his father's death, and ruled the kingdom."}},{"n":29,"text":"तथैवाहं मतिमता परिचिन्त्येह पाण्डुना ।\nज्येष्ठः प्रभ्रंशितो राज्याद्धीनाङ्ग इति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way, after the wise Pandu considered it here, I, the eldest, was removed from the kingdom as defective in body."}},{"n":30,"text":"पाण्डुस्तु राज्यं संप्राप्तः कनीयानपि सन्नृपः ।\nविनाशे तस्य पुत्राणामिदं राज्यमरिंदम ।\nमय्यभागिनि राज्याय कथं त्वं राज्यमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pandu, though younger, became king and obtained the kingdom. Now this kingdom belongs to his sons, tamer of foes; I am no sharer in the kingdom, so how can you want it?"}},{"n":31,"text":"युधिष्ठिरो राजपुत्रो महात्मा\nन्यायागतं राज्यमिदं च तस्य ।\nस कौरवस्यास्य जनस्य भर्ता\nप्रशासिता चैव महानुभावः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, the great-souled prince, holds this kingdom by right. He is the protector and ruler of this Kaurava people, of great power."}},{"n":32,"text":"स सत्यसंधः सतताप्रमत्तः\nशास्त्रे स्थितो बन्धुजनस्य साधुः ।\nप्रियः प्रजानां सुहृदानुकम्पी\nजितेन्द्रियः साधुजनस्य भर्ता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Always true to his word and ever alert, firm in the scriptures, good to his kin, dear to the people, kind to friends, compassionate, master of his senses, protector of the good,"}},{"n":33,"text":"क्षमा तितिक्षा दम आर्जवं च\nसत्यव्रतत्वं श्रुतमप्रमादः ।\nभूतानुकम्पा ह्यनुशासनं च\nयुधिष्ठिरे राजगुणाः समस्ताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"forbearance, endurance, self-control, uprightness, a vow of truth, learning, vigilance, compassion for creatures, and good governance: all the royal qualities are in Yudhishthira."}},{"n":34,"text":"अराजपुत्रस्त्वमनार्यवृत्तो\nलुब्धस्तथा बन्धुषु पापबुद्धिः ।\nक्रमागतं राज्यमिदं परेषां\nहर्तुं कथं शक्ष्यसि दुर्विनीतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are no prince, your conduct is ignoble, you are greedy and evil-minded toward your kin. Ill-bred as you are, how will you be able to seize this kingdom that has come down to others by succession?"}},{"n":35,"text":"प्रयच्छ राज्यार्धमपेतमोहः\nसवाहनं त्वं सपरिच्छदं च ।\nततोऽवशेषं तव जीवितस्य\nसहानुजस्यैव भवेन्नरेन्द्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"Free from delusion, give half the kingdom, with its vehicles and its furnishings. Then the rest of your life, King, will be left to you and your younger brothers.\""}}]}]}